{"surah": 93, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "وَٱلضُّحَىٰ ", "translation": "By the morning brightness", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلضُّحَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَḥُّḍlٱَw", "root": "ضحو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَٱلَّيْلِ إِذَا سَجَىٰ ", "translation": "And [by] the night when it covers with darkness,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّيْلِ", "translit": "ِlْyَّlٱَw", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَجَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَjgَs", "root": "سجو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "مَا وَدَّعَكَ رَبُّكَ وَمَا قَلَىٰ ", "translation": "Your Lord has not taken leave of you, [O Muḥammad], nor has He detested [you].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَدَّعَكَ", "translit": "َkَʿعَّdَw", "root": "ودع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَq", "root": "قلي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَلَلْءَاخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لَّكَ مِنَ ٱلْأُولَىٰ ", "translation": "And the Hereafter is better for you than the first [life].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَلْءَاخِرَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَrِhkāَءْlَlَw", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَيْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأُولَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlwُaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَلَسَوْفَ يُعْطِيكَ رَبُّكَ فَتَرْضَىٰٓ ", "translation": "And your Lord is going to give you, and you will be satisfied.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَسَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَsَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُعْطِيكَ", "translit": "َkyِṭْʿعُy", "root": "عطو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَتَرْضَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَḍْrَtَf", "root": "رضو"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "أَلَمْ يَجِدْكَ يَتِيمًا فَـَٔاوَىٰ ", "translation": "Did He not find you an orphan and give [you] refuge?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَجِدْكَ", "translit": "َkْdِjgَy", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَتِيمًا", "translit": "āًmyِtَy", "root": "يتم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَـَٔاوَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَwāَٔـَf", "root": "اوي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَوَجَدَكَ ضَآلًّا فَهَدَىٰ ", "translation": "And He found you lost and guided [you],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَوَجَدَكَ", "translit": "َkَdَjgَwَw", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ضَآلًّا", "translit": "āًّlٓāَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَهَدَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَdَhَf", "root": "هدي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "وَوَجَدَكَ عَآئِلًا فَأَغْنَىٰ ", "translation": "And He found you poor and made [you] self-sufficient.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَوَجَدَكَ", "translit": "َkَdَjgَwَw", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَآئِلًا", "translit": "āًlِyʾٓāَʿع", "root": "عيل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَأَغْنَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَnْغَaʾَf", "root": "غني"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "فَأَمَّا ٱلْيَتِيمَ فَلَا تَقْهَرْ ", "translation": "So as for the orphan, do not oppress [him].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْيَتِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِtَyْlٱ", "root": "يتم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَقْهَرْ", "translit": "ْrَhْqَt", "root": "قهر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَأَمَّا ٱلسَّآئِلَ فَلَا تَنْهَرْ ", "translation": "And as for the petitioner,[1] do not repel [him].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسَّآئِلَ", "translit": "َlِyʾٓāَّslٱ", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَنْهَرْ", "translit": "ْrَhْnَt", "root": "نهر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "وَأَمَّا بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ فَحَدِّثْ ", "translation": "But as for the favor of your Lord, report [it].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِنِعْمَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَmْʿعِnِb", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَحَدِّثْ", "translit": "ْhtِّdَḥَf", "root": "حدث"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"5": [{"arabic": "وفي تفسير قوله تعالى {ولسوف يعطيك ربك فترضى} قال لا يرضى محمد وواحد من أمته في النار وكان أبو جعفر محمد بن علي يقول أنتم أهل العراق تقولون أرجى آية في كتاب الله عز وجل قوله {قل يا عبادي الذين أسرفوا على أنفسهم لا تقنطوا من رحمة الله} الآية ونحن أهل البيت نقول أرجى آية في كتاب الله تعالى قوله تعالى {ولسوف يعطيك ربك فترضى} وأما الأخبار فقد روى أبو موسى عنه صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال أمتي أمة مرحومة لا عذاب عليها في الآخرة عجل الله عقابها في الدنيا الزلازل والفتن فإذا كان يوم القيامة دفع إلى كل رجل من أمتي", "english": "So it was said to him: \"And what is in it of hope?\" He said: \"This world, all of it, is little, and a man's provision from it is little, and his religion is little in comparison to his provision. So look at how God Most High sent down in it the longest verse, to guide His servant to the path of caution in preserving his wealth — so how could He not preserve his religion, which has no substitute for him?\"", "book_title": "Remembrance of Death and Afterlife", "section_title_ar": "Section 1033", "section_title_en": "The Book of Hope (Kitāb al-Rajā') — Section 1033: The Second Art — Surveying the Verses and Reports Concerning Hope", "section_index": 1033, "anchors": "- Root: وجود (w-j-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of \"finding\" and \"existence\"; here in the sense of what is present and available.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Existence as that which is found and realized; in theological context, the given order of creation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) sense of \"being found\"; metaphorical (majāz) extension to the entirety of created things.\n- Root: رجا (r-j-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To hope, to expect with desire; the opposite of despair (ya's).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Hope as a theological virtue — the heart's expectation of divine mercy, balanced against fear (khawf).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: expectation of a desired outcome; metaphorical: the soul's reliance on divine generosity.\n- Root: غفر (gh-f-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To cover, to shield, to pardon; the root implies veiling the fault.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Divine forgiveness as the covering of sins and the effacing of their consequence.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: covering; metaphorical: God's remission of punishment.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — used to emphasize exclusive attributes of divine mercy and forgiveness.", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the journey of the soul, death, and the Hereafter, from 'Remembrance of Death and Afterlife'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "11": [{"arabic": "الرابع أن الإظهار إقامة لسنة الشكر وقد قال تعالى وأما بنعمة ربك فحدث والكتمان كفران النعمة وقد ذم الله عز وجل من كتم ما أتاه الله عز وجل وقرنه بالبخل فقال تعالى الذين يبخلون ويأمرون الناس بالبخل ويكتمون ما آتاهم الله من فضله وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم إذا أنعم الله علي عبد نعمة أحب أن ترى نعمته عليه (1) وأعطى رجل بعض الصالحين شيئا في السر فرفع به يده وقال هذا من الدنيا والعلانية فيها أفضل والسر في أمور الآخرة أفضل ولذلك قال بعضهم إذا أعطيت في الملأ فخذ ثم اردد في السر والشكر فيه محثوث عليه قال صلى الله عليه وسلم من لم يش", "english": "Abū Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī said: \"I indeed abandon wearing a new garment, fearing that it might engender envy in my neighbors.\" And one of the ascetics said: \"Perhaps I abandon the use of a thing for the sake of my brothers, lest they say: 'From where does he have this?'\" It is related of Ibrāhīm al-Taymī that a new shirt was seen upon him, and one of his brothers said: \"From where did you get this?\" He replied: \"My brother Khaythamah clothed me with it. Had I known that his family knew of it, I would not have accepted it.\"", "book_title": "Mysteries of Zakat", "section_title_ar": "Section 183", "section_title_en": "On Sincerity (Ikhlas): The Ethics of Giving and Receiving — Concealment versus Disclosure", "section_index": 183, "anchors": "- Root: س ت ر (s-t-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Covering, veiling, concealing; the act of screening something from view.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Concealment (sitr) preserves inviolability and prevents exposure of need, aligning with the Quranic description of the poor who \"restrain themselves\" so that the ignorant think them wealthy.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqiqah) — physical covering; Metaphorical (majaz) — concealing one's state of need or one's charitable act from the eyes of others.\n- Root: ظ ه ر (ẓ-h-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To become apparent, visible, manifest; the opposite of concealment.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Openness and manifestation; used for both physical visibility and the public disclosure of an act.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — making something perceptible to the senses; Metaphorical — publicizing one's good deeds, which carries both the virtue of gratitude and the peril of ostentation.\n- Root: ش ك ر (sh-k-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The core root denotes acknowledgment and increase; a beast \"shakur\" is one that thrives on little fodder.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"The perception of the blessing and its manifestation.\" It is the opposite of kufr (disbelief/ingratitude), which is the forgetting and covering of the blessing. It is of three types: of the heart (perceiving the blessing), of the tongue (praising the Benefactor), and of the limbs (rewarding the blessing with obedience).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — verbal praise of the benefactor; Metaphorical — the act of the one who, upon receiving a gift, openly expresses gratitude, which is a Sunnah, as in {«وَأَمَّا بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ فَحَدِّثْ»}.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The rule governing the separation of a preposition from its object for rhetorical emphasis, here applied to the nuanced interposition of intention (niyyah) between the outward act and its inward reality.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Mysteries of Zakat'", "badge": "Ethics"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 200, 1890]], "93:1": [[1, 200, 1890]], "2": [[1, 10, 1437], [2, 1437, 2442], [3, 2442, 3700]], "93:2": [[1, 10, 1437], [2, 1437, 2442], [3, 2442, 3700]], "3": [[1, 330, 1085], [2, 1085, 2391], [3, 2391, 3156], [4, 3156, 4401], [5, 4401, 5700]], "93:3": [[1, 330, 1085], [2, 1085, 2391], [3, 2391, 3156], [4, 3156, 4401], [5, 4401, 5700]], "4": [[1, 200, 2671], [2, 2671, 3525], [3, 3525, 4151], [4, 4151, 4607], [5, 4607, 6910]], "93:4": [[1, 200, 2671], [2, 2671, 3525], [3, 3525, 4151], [4, 4151, 4607], [5, 4607, 6910]], "5": [[1, 200, 1615], [2, 1615, 3270], [3, 3270, 4018], [4, 4018, 6300]], "93:5": [[1, 200, 1615], [2, 1615, 3270], [3, 3270, 4018], [4, 4018, 6300]], "6": [[1, 530, 1179], [2, 1179, 2334], [3, 2334, 4260], [4, 4260, 6380]], "93:6": [[1, 530, 1179], [2, 1179, 2334], [3, 2334, 4260], [4, 4260, 6380]], "7": [[1, 20, 1963], [2, 1963, 5401], [3, 5401, 7160]], "93:7": [[1, 20, 1963], [2, 1963, 5401], [3, 5401, 7160]], "8": [[1, 220, 1772], [2, 1772, 4627], [3, 4627, 6320]], "93:8": [[1, 220, 1772], [2, 1772, 4627], [3, 4627, 6320]], "9": [[1, 370, 1938], [2, 1938, 3738], [3, 3738, 4776], [4, 4776, 5760]], "93:9": [[1, 370, 1938], [2, 1938, 3738], [3, 3738, 4776], [4, 4776, 5760]], "10": [[1, 250, 1982], [2, 1982, 4768], [3, 4768, 5726], [4, 5726, 6520]], 